# Comparison of Deployment Strategies

| Strategy       | Downtime | Two Versions Running | Gradual Traffic Shift | Instant Rollback | Typical Use Case                                       |
| -------------- | -------- | -------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Recreate       | Yes      | No                   | No                    | No               | Simple internal applications                           |
| Rolling Update | No       | Temporarily          | No                    | Moderate         | Default Kubernetes deployment                          |
| Canary         | No       | Yes                  | Yes                   | Yes              | Validate new releases with a small percentage of users |
| Blue-Green     | No       | Yes                  | No (instant switch)   | Yes              | Production systems requiring fast rollback             |

---

# Production Perspective

Large organizations commonly use:

* Rolling Updates for regular application upgrades.
* Canary Deployments to validate risky changes with a small audience.
* Blue-Green Deployments for major releases where an immediate rollback is critical.

The strategy is chosen based on the application's risk, user impact, and operational requirements rather than one approach replacing all others.

